 plot of log (<italic>k/k</italic><italic><sub>o</sub></italic>) for isopropyl chloroformate (<bold>1</bold>) against log (<italic>k/k</italic><italic><sub>o</sub></italic>) for 2-adamantyl chloroformate (<bold>3</bold>) in pure and binary solvents at 25.0 &#x000ba;C.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ijms-10-00862f3"/></fig><fig id="f4-ijms-10-00862" position="float"><label>Scheme 1.</label><caption><p>Alcoholysis plus hydrolysis of phenyl chloroformate (<bold>4</bold>).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ijms-10-00862f4"/></fig><fig id="f5-ijms-10-00862" position="float"><label>Scheme 2.</label><caption><p>Solvolysis-decomposition of 1-adamantyl chloroformate (<bold>2</bold>).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ijms-10-00862f5"/></fig><fig id="f6-ijms-10-00862" position="float"><label>Scheme 3.</label><caption><p>Stepwise addition-elimination mechanism through a tetrahedral intermediate proposed for phenyl chloroformate (<bold>4</bold>).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ijms-10-00862f6"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-ijms-10-00862" position="float"><label>Table 1.</label><caption><p>Specific rates of solvolysis (<italic>k</italic>)<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn1-ijms-10-00862">a</xref> of <bold>1</bold>, in several binary solvents at 25.0 &#x000ba;C and 40.0 &#x000b0;C; literature values for (<italic>N</italic><italic><sub>T</sub></italic>) and (<italic>Y</italic><italic><sub>Cl</sub></italic>); and the percentages of overall reaction proceeding with acid formation at 40.0 &#x000b0;C.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Solvent (%)<italic><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn2-ijms-10-00862">b</xref></italic></bold></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>1 @ 25.0 &#x000b0;C; 10<sup>5</sup><italic>k</italic>, s<sup>&#x02212;1</sup></bold><italic><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn3-ijms-10-00862">c</xref>,<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn4-ijms-10-00862">d</xref></italic></th><th ali