 &#x000b0;C [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b46-ijms-10-00862">46</xref>].</p></fn><fn id="tfn11-ijms-10-00862"><label><sup>k</sup></label><p>Calculated from values at 25.3 &#x000b0;C, 33.0 &#x000b0;C, and 50.6 &#x000b0;C [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b47-ijms-10-00862">47</xref>].</p></fn><fn id="tfn12-ijms-10-00862"><label><sup>l</sup></label><p>Value for 100% HCOOH.</p></fn><fn id="tfn13-ijms-10-00862"><label><sup>m</sup></label><p>This study.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t2-ijms-10-00862" position="float"><label>Table 2.</label><caption><p>Subtraction of the calculated specific rate by the ionization mechanism (<italic>k</italic><sub>i</sub>) from the experimentally measured specific rates of reaction (<italic>k</italic>) at 40.0 &#x000b0;C and 25.0 &#x000b0;C.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Solvent (%)<italic><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn14-ijms-10-00862">a</xref></italic></bold></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>10<sup>5</sup><italic>k</italic>, s<sup>&#x02212;1</sup><italic><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn15-ijms-10-00862">b</xref></italic></bold></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>10<sup>5</sup><italic>k</italic><sub>i</sub>, s<sup>&#x02212;1</sup><italic><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn16-ijms-10-00862">c</xref></italic></bold></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>10<sup>5</sup> (<italic>k&#x02013;k</italic><sub>i</sub>), s<sup>&#x02212;1</sup></bold></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>10<sup>5</sup><italic>k</italic>, s<sup>&#x02212;1</sup><italic><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn18-ijms-10-00862">e</xref></italic></bold></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>10<sup>5</sup><italic>k</italic><sub>i</sub>, s<sup>&#x02212;1</sup><italic><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn19-ijms-10-00862">f</xref></italic></bold></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>10<